## Deferred: Metal renderer work items (2026-04-16)

### Status: parked — revisit after RE_AddPolyToScene is in.

---

### #2 — Batched RT_SPRITE into dynamic vertex buffer

**Why parked:** no bottleneck yet. Current frame has ~26 draw cmds, GPU 2.7–3.5ms
on A19 Pro. Optimize when we actually have a perf pin, not on speculation.

**Goal:** replace per-sprite draw calls with a single batched draw. Visually identical;
massive draw-call reduction.

**Design:**

```c
#define MAX_SPRITE_VERTS   8192
#define MAX_SPRITE_INDICES 12288

static SpriteVertex s_spriteVerts[MAX_SPRITE_VERTS];
static uint16_t     s_spriteIndices[MAX_SPRITE_INDICES];
static int          s_spriteVertCount = 0;
static int          s_spriteIndexCount = 0;
```

Per-sprite: build camera-facing quad from `origin`, `radius`, camera `right/up`
vectors; append 4 verts + 6 indices (two triangles). Clear counts in `RE_ClearScene`.
Single `drawIndexedPrimitives` at end-of-frame:

```swift
setVertexBuffer(spriteVerts)
setIndexBuffer(spriteIndices)
setBlendMode(ADDITIVE)       // src=ONE, dst=ONE
depthWriteEnabled = false
drawIndexedPrimitives(type: .triangle, indexCount: s_spriteIndexCount)
```

**Texture handling:**
- Minimal: assume one texture (tracer/muzzle flash dominant case).
- Better: group by texture, one draw per group.

**Debug:** `Com_Printf("[DBG] spriteVerts=%d spriteIdx=%d\n", ...)`.

**Expected gain:** same visuals, one draw call instead of N. Stable perf headroom
for Vision Pro stereo later.

