## Deferred: per-vertex normals attribute (entity pipeline)

**Context:** entity vertices currently do NOT carry a per-vertex normal. CPU-side
Lambert in `RE_RenderScene` decodes MD3 lat/long normals and bakes
`(ambient + directed * NdotL) * entityColor` into `vertex.color`.

**Why revisit:** if we later want per-pixel lighting (normal mapping, specular,
env reflections), we'll need normals as a real vertex attribute, not pre-baked.

**Design:** add `normal: float3` to `Q3MetalEntityVertex`, emit from MD3 build
loop, pass through `q3_entity_vertex` to `q3_entity_fragment`. Drop the baked
color Lambert in favor of per-pixel NdotL.
